card.statement:
Note that for this automorphism to be involutive we need $
u$ to be $( eta,\sigma)$ -admissible and that the automorphism $	au$ depends on the shape.

Our present goal is to give a complete description of the Dirac reduction $R(^{
u}y_{n}(\sigma),	au)$ . Before doing so we will state the relationship between $R(^{
u}y_{n}(\sigma),	au)$ , $R(^{\mu}y_{n}(\sigma),	au)$ where both $\mu$ and $
u$ are $( eta,\sigma)$ -admissble.
